{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Pharaoh said, etc.</b> The meaning is: because they are many, they cannot (I Kings 7:26) — it is not within their capacity — for all of them to remove from themselves this faintness of heart occasioned by the threat of the sword, and this matter will cause you to interrupt them from their labors, for their courage will ferment and take courage, and this outcry is directed against Moses and Aaron. Or he may argue against the taskmasters who allowed them to come to Pharaoh and suspended their work, and he said that since they are indeed many, even a brief time of suspended work will make a great impact."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:45.018943689Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}